{{Quote|We are approaching the planet Yavin. The Rebel base is on a moon on the far side. We are preparing to orbit the planet.|An [[Imperial officer]], to Imperial [[Grand Moff]] [[Wilhuff Tarkin]], via intercom|<ref name="Episode IV">{{Film|IV}}</ref>}}
'''Yavin Prime''',<ref name="Jedi Fallen Order">''[[Star Wars Jedi: Fallen Order]]''</ref> also known simply as '''Yavin''',<ref name="Episode IV" /> was an [[Color|orange]] [[gas giant]], nearly 200,000 [[kilometer]]s in diameter,<ref name="ANH junior" /> located in the [[Outer Rim Territories]].<ref name="Ultimate Star Wars" /> Its clouds provided cover in battle, but [[death]] awaited any pilot who dove too far.<ref name="Squadrons">''[[Star Wars: Squadrons]]''</ref>

It was [[orbit]]ed by twenty-six [[moon]]s,<ref name="TUVG" /> three of which could sustain [[humanoid]] life,<ref name="ANH junior" /> including [[Yavin 4]], [[Yavin 8]], and [[Yavin 13]].<ref name="HC4" /> One of those moons, [[Yavin 4]], was once home to the ancient [[Massassi]] [[Soldier|warriors]]<ref name="Ultimate Star Wars" /> and was used by the [[Alliance to Restore the Republic|Rebel Alliance]].<ref name="Episode IV" />

The primary [[Hyperspace route|hyperlane]] used to reach Yavin was the [[Hydian Way]]; its trace hyperlanes included the [[Pinooran Spur]], the [[Junction-Tierell Loop]], and the [[Yavin Bypass]].<ref name="Rebel Files">''[[Star Wars: The Rebel Files]]''</ref>

==History==
{{Quote|Orbiting the planet at maximum velocity. The moon with the Rebel base will be in range in thirty minutes.|An Imperial officer, to Imperial Grand Moff Wilhuff Tarkin, via intercom|<ref name="Episode IV" />}}
[[File:YavinPrime-AORCR.png|thumb|left|200px|Yavin Prime orbited by several of its moons]]
In the [[Standard year|year]] [[1 BBY]],<ref name="GA">''[[Star Wars: Galactic Atlas: Updated Edition]]''</ref> the ''[[Millennium Falcon]]'' [[orbit]]ed the [[gas giant]] to reach [[Yavin 4]], where the [[Great Temple|headquarters]] for the [[Alliance to Restore the Republic]] were located. Later, Yavin 4 was almost destroyed by the [[DS-1 Orbital Battle Station|Death Star]], a [[planet]]-[[Death|killing]] [[battle station]] designed by the [[Galactic Empire]], but the Death Star was [[Battle of Yavin|destroyed]] by [[Luke Skywalker]].<ref name="Episode IV" />

Four years after the [[Destruction of Alderaan|destruction]] of [[Alderaan]], [[Captain]] [[Wedge Antilles]] and [[Vanguard Squadron]] were sent on a mission to Yavin Prime, to [[Battle of Yavin Prime|steal]] the [[Imperial-class Star Destroyer|''Imperial''-class Star Destroyer]] ''[[Victorum]]'', which was already in an engagement with [[Talus Group]]. The [[Star Destroyer]] was needed for the [[New Republic]]'s secret [[Project Starhawk]].<ref name="Squadrons" />

{{Planet-stub}}

==Behind the scenes==
The gas giant Yavin first appeared in [[Star Wars: Episode IV A New Hope|''Star Wars:'' Episode IV A ''New Hope'']], the first ''[[Star Wars]]'' film.<ref name="Episode IV" />

The ''[[Star Wars: Rogue One: The Ultimate Visual Guide|Rogue One Ultimate Visual Guide]] ''states that Yavin has twenty-six moons.<ref name="TUVG" /> However, [[Star Wars: Complete Locations (2016)|''Star Wars: Complete Locations'']] states that the planet has thirteen moons.<ref name="Star Wars: Complete Locations (2016)">[[Star Wars: Complete Locations (2016)|''Star Wars: Complete Locations'']]</ref>

